# M05 Gen2 console session — read-only live recheck

- Captured: 2026-09-24 17:15:31–17:15:32 UTC (guest reports 17:15:32 UTC).
- Scope: bounded SSH read-only queries to the existing Gen2 guest, authenticated as `sa`; no admin login, GUI/Plasma command, or guest write was attempted.
- SSH alias: `alp-m2-gen2` resolves in the local config to stale `172.28.171.21`.
- Endpoint override: `ssh -T -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=6 -o ConnectionAttempts=1 -o HostName=172.28.164.164 alp-m2-gen2 '<read-only query>'`; only the endpoint was overridden, preserving alias user/key settings.
- The single remote shell query ran `date -u`, `hostname`, printed `$SSH_CONNECTION`, read `/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id`, ran `loginctl list-sessions --no-legend`, iterated admin sessions with `loginctl show-session` for the properties below, filtered current-boot journal lines for the login PAM session, checked `systemctl is-enabled` and `is-active` for the three named units, counted `systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager`, then probed `command -v ip` and `ip -brief address`.
- Local SSH process exit status: `0`.

